            <ArticleTitle>A giant left atrial myxoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>819052</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1155/2014/819052</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atrial myxomas are the most common primary cardiac tumors. Patients with left atrial myxomas generally present with mechanical obstruction of blood flow, systemic embolization, and constitutional symptoms. We present a case of an unusually large left atrial myxoma discovered incidentally in a patient with longstanding dyspnea being managed as bronchial asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
